These are important for practical exams because they use `Length`, `Substring()`, `Replace()`, `ToUpper()`, `Split()` and loops.

## 17. Reverse a string using `for`

```
using System;

class Program
{
    static void Main()
    {
        Console.Write("Enter a string: ");
        string s = Console.ReadLine();

        string rev = "";

        for (int i = s.Length - 1; i >= 0; i--)
            rev += s[i];

        Console.WriteLine("Reverse = " + rev);
        Console.ReadLine();
    }
}
```

## 18. Check whether a string is a palindrome

